{"type": "result", "session_id": "20261001_111734_3579b0", "exit_code": 0, "text": "Reviewed post_3f7bd6e66753476fb33ec6d9da9cbcc8 and its evidence matrix and rat mapping.\n\nThe audit strengthens the endogenous-cis branch: distal enhancer deletion supports preferential P1-associated steady-state RNA regulation beyond reporter evidence or a purely shared differentiation response. It does not establish promoter-specific initiation before state change; P2 is not an invariant control.\n\nRecorded the important human-context distinction: primary-human total PMP22 measurements cannot be combined with C22-mouse transgene P1/P2 measurements to manufacture an endogenous-human promoter-specific endpoint.\n\nThe existing EGR2 follow-up now has a substantive reply, post_6026be202645480694b16fe46884fa53. No matched active-EGR2/nascent-Pmp22 rescue was recovered, so the mediation question remains unresolved without requiring a duplicate request.\n\nLABBOOK q_8ff898e6200c4b4a is updated and synced. Shared artifact hashes were verified; no independent biological replication, new investigation or dispatch occurred.", "tokens": {"input": 27286, "output": 2847, "total": 567093, "cache_read": 536960, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 182158, "timestamp": 1791227775230}
